dot_emacs Repository Version History
====================================

v26.08 (Release Date: TBD)
--------------------------
- Add .gitattributes, marking the Markdown documents for diff and the
  vendored third-party README files as vendored.
- Expand doc/GUIDELINES with the document file naming and attribute
  recommendations, the reach of a compatibility bridge and when a bundled
  file may be edited instead, the scope and history of a pull request, the
  width a version history entry keeps, and when an executable script's own
  version is updated.
- Add the terminating period to the Policy header line of dot_emacs and the
  doc/GUIDELINES example.
- Wrap the lines of this file at 75 columns.
- Add the shared version history description guidelines to the end of this
  file.
- Replace count-lines-region, removed in Emacs 29, with count-lines in
  sws-mode.el, so indenting a region in sws-mode and jade-mode works again.
- Require core-compat-bridge when compiling auto-save-buffers-enhanced.el,
  so its toggle-read-only call no longer warns.
- Silence the native compilation warning pop-up in init.el, keeping the
  entries in the *Warnings* buffer.
- Declare the conditionally defined and optional mmm-mode functions of the
  bundled browse-kill-ring.el, minibuf-isearch.el and
  auto-save-buffers-enhanced.el, so the compiler no longer reports them as
  unknown.
- Absorb the obsolete cl aliases in cl-compat-bridge.el, so the bundled
  files that still load cl stop reporting every call.
- Describe each main directory in the README Directory Structure section.
- Clarify the license exclusions for the bundled third-party software.
- Replace jaspace with the standard whitespace mode, enabled globally, and
  remove the bundled jaspace.el, whose display table showed an ASCII @ as a
  box.
- Complete byte-compilation coverage for active DOT_EMACS modules.

v26.07 (2026-07-31)
-------------------
- Resolve the installer script directory before changing the working
  directory, so relative invocations work.
- Byte-compile with the elisp load path, so bundled files requiring the
  compatibility bridges are compiled.
- Allow nosudo installs and uninstalls to run when the sudo command is
  unavailable.
- Add -n and --no-sudo aliases for the installer and uninstaller.
- Replace awk {n,} interval expression in usage() with a portable
  equivalent for mawk compatibility.
- Build the bundled helm only on Emacs 24 through 26, where it is actually
  loaded, since its Makefile fails on newer Emacs.
- Drop the unreachable adaptive history cleanup from the uninstaller.
- Declare my-load-path with defvar in init.el before assigning it.
- Fix the dired-async loader so dired-async-mode is enabled at startup.
- Simplify the redundant timidity autoload wrapper in autoloads.el.
- Fix the recentf-ext-settings.el load typo and clean up two obsolete
  autoload entries.
- Remove the unused auto-save-buffers block from autoloads.el, which could
  double up with auto-save-buffers-enhanced.
- Remove the obsolete default-major-mode setting, which no longer affects
  the major mode of new buffers.
- Add a quiet argument to load-p and use it for the optional site-lisp
  loader, which reported a failure on every startup.
- Stay quiet about the italk, mic-paren, and develock loaders, which are
  not bundled and failed on every startup.
- Disable the blinking cursor explicitly, since a nil argument now enables
  the mode instead of toggling it.
- Replace the obsolete find-file-hooks alias with find-file-hook in
  configs.el.
- Set temporary-file-directory to /dev/shm only on GNU/Linux, since
  platforms such as macOS have no such directory.
- Stop redefining the built-in previous-buffer, and bind M-n to a new
  forward-buffer command instead.
- Turn off hl-line in toggle-view-mode by calling hl-line-mode instead of
  assigning to its variable.
- Disable the malformed view-mode "." key entry, which signalled a commandp
  error instead of running a command.
- Require dired in dired-settings.el, which relied on another library to
  load dired-mode-map first.
- Apply the navi2ch proxy user and password only when the proxy is enabled.
- Fix with-suppressed-message so message-log-max is bound at run time
  instead of macro expansion time.
- Require cl-compat-bridge instead of the obsolete cl package in
  multi-term-settings.el.
- Bridge the legacy CL names cl-lib provides only with a cl- prefix, such
  as first, block, return, getf and subseq, which broke Rinari loading and
  C-x b on Emacs 30.
- Add a lexical-let* shim next to the existing lexical-let one, which
  anything-config.el and other bundled files still use.
- Give dolist and dotimes an implicit nil block, so legacy return calls
  keep working without the obsolete cl package.
- Guard set-face-bold-p calls in faces.el with fboundp to avoid breaking
  font-lock-mode-hook if the obsolete function is removed.
- Guard screen.el against an unset TERM environment variable to avoid a
  string-match error on startup.
- Drop the redundant .el suffix from the markdown-mode autoload-p call in
  lang-mode.el for consistency.
- Remove the bundled shadow.el and its settings, which collided with the
  built-in shadow.el and broke find-file.
- Remove the unused new-file-p.el and the bundled foreign-regexp.el, which
  are no longer loaded.
- Remove web-mode-settings.el, whose indentation settings used web-mode 7
  variable names that web-mode 8 ignores.
- Require scala-mode-auto optionally in lang-mode.el, since a missing
  scala-mode aborted the rest of the startup.
- Keep the built-in gensym in cl-compat-bridge.el instead of aliasing it to
  cl-gensym.
- Stop calling viewer-stay-in-setup twice in view-mode-key.el, and provide
  the feature under the file name.
- Add to python-mode-hook and gtags-mode-hook instead of replacing them, so
  other settings survive.
- Replace quoted lambdas in hooks and timers with plain ones, which lexical
  binding turns into closures.
- Compare emacs-major-version against plain numbers instead of quoted ones.
- Correct the toggle-read-only comment in core-compat-bridge.el, which
  described the shim as being for old Emacs.

